# Uncommitted session log

Maintain `.cursor/uncommitted.md` for work that is **not committed yet**.

Skip this when `git status` is clean.

## Format

Numbered list only. Prefix each item with `Feature:`, `Update:`, or `Removal:`:

```
# Uncommitted

1. Feature: …
2. Update: …
3. Removal: …
```

No essays, diffs, or file lists.

## Keep it high level

Describe the outcome, not the implementation. If a teammate reading the release note would not care, leave it out.

Tiny UX (copy-to-clipboard, chip layout, hover, padding, icon tweaks) stays off the list.

## Compress — one line per feature area

Prefer **fewer, fuller lines** over many thin ones. Same session, same user-facing area → **one line**.

- **Feature + follow-up updates** to that feature → merge into the original `Feature:` line (semicolon-separated clauses).
- **Several updates** in the same area (e.g. bug list polish + bug filters + bug filing) → one `Feature:` or `Update:` line covering all outcomes.
- **Do not omit work** — every user-facing change stays in the log; compression merges lines, it does not drop items.
- Unrelated areas (ticket form vs leaderboard vs digest) stay on separate lines.

When appending mid-session, **edit an existing line** if the change belongs to that feature area; add a new line only for a distinct area.

## When to append

After you add, change, or delete behavior a user would notice (code, seed, schema).

Never log:

- Implementation detail — markup, accessibility wiring, naming, refactors, file moves
- Documentation — `AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md`, `README`, comments
- Agent config — `.cursor/rules/*`, skills, hooks, rule imports
- Format-only edits, `prisma generate`, dependency lock churn

Fold sub-steps into the feature they serve rather than listing them separately.

## When to clear

After a successful commit of that work, reset the file to:

```
# Uncommitted

(none)
```

Use skill `barmijly-prepare-commit` then `barmijly-commit` when the user asks to commit — commit includes this reset.

## Chat

Do **not** paste the full log at the end of a turn.

If this turn **added or edited** a line in `.cursor/uncommitted.md`, quote only that line (or those lines). If this turn did not change the log, omit it from the reply.
